## Context

Charter #444 (stale-leaf GC on re-plan) has two implementation leaves:
- **#448 (444-gc-impl)**: adds a nested `cst=needs-plan` GC guard to
  `/work/reference/runtime/crewboss-launcher-gh.sh` with a `numsAfter` numeric-equality filter.
- **#449 (444-gc-test)**: writes `gc-stale-leaves.test.sh` with two-charter prefix isolation
  (charters #5 and #50) and updates manifest counters.

This leaf reviews both PRs for correctness and merges them once all checks pass.

## Task

Review the PRs opened by leaves #448 and #449. Verify all of the following before approving:

### (a) Nested guard placement — impl PR

In `/work/reference/runtime/crewboss-launcher-gh.sh`, the GC logic must be inside a **nested**
`if [ "$cst" = "needs-plan" ]; then … fi` block that sits within the compound success block
at line 913 (`if [ "$_plok" = "true" ] || [ "$cst" = "needs-plan" ]; then`).

Confirm the GC code is NOT reachable when `_plok=true` (plan:agreed path).  If it fires on
plan:agreed it would close the freshly-created correct leaves before launch.

### (b) Word-boundary-safe filter — impl PR

The jq predicate for identifying stale leaves must use `numsAfter` + numeric equality (or
an equivalent regex with word-boundary: `test("Charter: #" + ($cid|tostring) + "([^0-9]|$)")`).

Specifically confirm: if `$id = 5`, the filter does NOT match a leaf whose body contains
`Charter: #50`.  A bare `contains("Charter: #5")` substring match would fail this test.

### (c) Prefix-isolation scenario — test PR

`gc-stale-leaves.test.sh` must contain Scenario B: two charters seeded with IDs **#5** and
**#50** (string-prefix pair), stale leaves for each, needs-plan triggered for #5 only.
Assertions must cover: #5 leaf CLOSED AND #50 leaf remains OPEN.

### (d) Manifest counter updates — test PR

Confirm all four of:
1. `leaf-verifier.test.sh` line 266: `[ "$_excl_count" -eq 51 ]` (was 50)
2. `leaf-verifier.test.sh` line 270: `[ "$_actual_count" -eq 71 ]` (was 70)
3. `per-leaf-manifest` line 17 header: `ALLOW=20, EXCLUDED=51, union=71`
4. `per-leaf-manifest` EXCLUDED section: entry for `gc-stale-leaves` present

### (e) SHA manifest — test PR

`runtime-manifest.tsv` has updated SHA rows for every canonical runtime file changed in both PRs.

### (f) verify-merged ALL-GREEN

Run `reference/tests/verify-merged.sh`.  All tests must pass (no FAIL lines, exit 0).

